  "signatures": {
    "$comment": "Recipes are toppings only. The yogurt is the customer's choice: bowls carry no default, smoothies default to defaultBase.smoothies unless the item sets its own `base` (The Recovery: High Protein 0%). 2026-09-10 (owner, from Kim's Uber Eats submission): the delivery menu became the store menu. The Bloom is back in The Seasonal's place with its 2026-08-28 recipe (toasted and shredded coconut are one ingredient now, so the recipe and its figures are unchanged); The Seasonal is retired to docs/menu/retired-items.md. The Tropics is The Tropic again and lost goji berries, so its figures are the pre-2026-08-28 ones. The Cabana, The Glow and The Sea Greens (The Coral until today, whey water now printed as an ingredient at 140 mL) lost honey. The Recovery moved to the High Protein base. Every changed smoothie was recomputed from Kim's gram weights (Smoothie Recipes sheet, PDF pp. 2-3) with the per-100 g values of the macro sheets; the working is meros-macros-sheets/2026-09-10_Smoothies_v3.csv. One weight the sheet leaves blank is assumed there and flagged: The Glow's raspberries (80 g, Marie's). 2026-09-10, later the same day (owner): The Recovery takes whey protein isolate and peanut butter back, the two it carried in the original Meros workbook recipe, and the collagen Kim's sheet had put in its place comes out. The High Protein base stays. 2026-09-11 (owner, tasted): the peanut butter comes out again, it does not mix with the acai; the whey and the base stand. The Recovery's figures are the only ones on this menu not computed from Kim's sheet: 436 kcal / 48 g protein, the sheet's remaining rows less collagen plus whey isolate at 30 g (Enhancers); the working is the same v3 CSV. The Crave is sold in store only (delivery.excludes). 2026-09-11 (owner): The Crave's whey protein isolate becomes chocolate whey protein isolate, a new registry ingredient, and the Canadian maple syrup comes out (the chocolate whey carries the sweetness). The raw cocoa powder came out with it and went straight back in the same day, so it stands. Its figures are the 2026-09-04 v2 sheet's rows less maple syrup (15 g, 39.000 / 0.000): 687 kcal / 42 g protein. CAVEAT: the chocolate whey carries plain whey isolate's per-scoop values until someone reads the tub's panel, so it is nutritionStatus needs-label like the plain one; a chocolate isolate usually runs a little higher in carbs and calories and a gram or two lower in protein, so 675/41 is the floor on calories. Bowl figures were computed with the yogurt each recipe named before 2026-08-28 (The Moment: Plain; the rest: Vanilla); a different base moves them by roughly 20 kcal / 1 g between the Greek yogurts. Peanut butter, chocolate and coconut milk are in no recipe and on no step; the validator warns, and pulling them is a separate decision. Peanut butter is still carried and is still in The Silk's peanut butter mousse, which is a different registry ingredient. Photography, 2026-09-10: every signature's photo is from the Uber Eats shoot of 2026-09-09 (MEROS-resources, resized into public/images-web/Signature/<id>.jpg; the TV's square crops are ../menu-tv/product-images/<Key>.jpg). transparent is optional and kept only where the top-down cut-out still matches the bowl as built (The Moment, The Silk); the other cut-outs predate the recipe changes. 2026-09-14 (owner): The Recovery takes peanut butter powder, a new registry ingredient (id pb-powder) distinct from the whole peanut butter pulled 2026-09-11 (that did not mix with the acai; powder mixes). Both would print as \"Peanut Butter,\" so the old, still-unused whole-butter entry (id peanut-butter; distinct from The Silk's peanut butter mousse) is renamed \"Peanut Butter (Whole)\" in the registry to keep the two apart; the id is unchanged so nothing that resolves it breaks. Figures move to 481 kcal / 53 g protein: the standing 436/48 plus the powder's 45 kcal / 5 g (2 tbsp, needs-label, no macro-sheet source yet). 2026-09-16 (owner): the whey protein isolate is grass fed, so both registry entries are renamed to \"Grass Fed Whey Protein\" and \"Chocolate Grass Fed Whey Protein\". Owner dropped \"Isolate\" from the printed name the same day, having first asked for it kept; the product is unchanged and both ids still say isolate. NOTE: isolate is what distinguishes this from a concentrate, which is the question lactose-sensitive customers ask, and the board no longer answers it; ids are unchanged, and the name carries to every surface that offers the enhancer, the Rebuild Stack and the delivery single-enhancer line, because it is one tub. The Crave moves to the High Protein 0% Fat base alongside The Recovery, and the two are pulled to the foot of the smoothie list under a new optional \"section\" field (\"High Protein\"), which the Menu TV and the website print as a group header; The Recovery drops its \"High Protein\" tag, now said once by the header. The Crave's figures move to 609 kcal / 53 g protein: the 2026-09-11 sum (686.501 / 42.352) less vanilla Greek at 200 g (188.941 / 7.347) plus high protein 0% at 200 g (111.406 / 17.632); the working is appended to meros-macros-sheets/2026-09-10_Smoothies_v3.csv. The strained base values fall well below the per-cup panel numbers in this registry, so the swap takes calories down, not up. 2026-09-18 (owner, from the board photo taken in store): the smoothie roster is re-costed end to end against the board, and the liquid is the headline. Every smoothie was computed on 120 g of filtered water at zero calories; the board makes it house whey water at 250 to 300 mL, which is +106 to +127 kcal before anything else moves, and it is most of the increase below. Honey returns to The Cabana, The Glow, The Sea Greens and The Recovery, reversing the 2026-09-10 removal, and Canadian maple syrup returns to The Crave, reversing the 2026-09-11 removal. Whey water now prints on no smoothie (owner): it is a liquid base like the yogurt, not a topping, so The Sea Greens drops it from its recipe and house-whey-water is left in the registry carrying no recipe and no step, which the validator warns about by design. Chia in The Glow and The Focus is a berry chia pudding spooned into the bottom of the cup and never blended, so it becomes its own registry ingredient (berry-chia-pudding, nuts-seeds) and prints under that name; The Cabana's plain soaked chia stays chia-seeds. Flaky Salt is renamed Sea Salt and the id is renamed with it (flaky-salt -> sea-salt), the owner's call that the store carries one salt; legacyIdMap keeps both old spellings pointing at the new id. Plain yogurt rim, ice and the blend passes are deliberately not printed on any surface. Figures are recomputed from the board's household measures converted to grams, same method and same per-100 g basis as the v3 sheet; the working is meros-macros-sheets/2026-09-18_Smoothies_v4.csv, which carries the conversion used on every row. The house scoop is 10 g, not the 30 g product scoop the recipe book's dose table still states (owner, 2026-09-18), so The Recovery takes 10 g of whey and The Crave 20 g; that alone is why both High Protein items fall, The Recovery 53 -> 39 g and The Crave 53 -> 43 g. They still run roughly double the rest of the roster, so the High Protein header stands. The Crave's liquid is cold brew, not the whey water the board offers as an alternate (owner); whey water instead would add about 106 kcal. CAVEAT: the berry chia pudding's berry soak is unweighed, so its entry carries the chia at 18 g only and is nutritionStatus needs-recipe. CAVEAT: MEROS-resources/04-recipes/15-recipe-book.md is stale against this roster (it still has chocolate and cacao nibs in The Crave, coconut milk and no whey in The Cabana, and smoothie liquid at 120 mL) and needs regenerating from this file.",
